@4 squinted.
While he was expecting to see the spires of some distant town or the smoke of a chandler's hearth fire at the twist of the road, he was surprised to see instead a greyish lump settled near a clump of young trees.
"Have you ever heard of a grey dragon, @0?" @4 asked.
@0 shook his head. "No, why?"
"Because that's what may be at the end of this road," @4 replied. "Feeling brave? We can go and have a closer look."�

entries.translation:
@4瞇起了眼。
原本他以為轉過這道彎，會看見遠方城鎮的尖塔，或是燭匠爐火的炊煙，沒想到眼前卻是一叢幼樹旁，一塊灰撲撲的隆起。
「@0，你聽過灰龍嗎？」@4問道。
@0搖了搖頭。「沒有，怎麼了？」
「因為這條路的盡頭，可能就是牠，」@4回答。「有膽量嗎？我們可以過去仔細瞧瞧。」�

這座石像十分巨大。
@5繞著底座走著，忍不住讚嘆龍背蜿蜒的曲線，通身覆滿了斜切的鱗片。他繞過那生物的尾巴，喊@3過來一起看，卻被男孩藍眼中那抹陰霾嚇了一跳。
「怎麼了嗎？」@5問道。
@3倒抽了一口氣，似乎想說些什麼，卻只是朝石像做了個手勢，便癱倒在地……�

entries.source:
The man accepted their company.
@0 chatted idly with the rough looking fellow as @1 looked on, making certain that in his ebullient mood the magician didn't slip and give away the true purpose of their travels.
"So, where are you headed?" the man asked, describing a large arc with his ale cup. "Anyplace interesting?"
"Actually, we're not headed in any ñspecific direction," @1 intervened. "We're wandering. Looking for an employer. Treasure to watch, caravan to guard..."
The man snickered. "Or a caravan to steal from, eh? Freebooters then. Well, there's not much going on in the Kingdom these days, not in the west. The Prince has seen to it his roads are safe and his vassals happy. For the likes of us, he's taken all the fun out of life."
@4 nodded. "You're not the first one to say so."�

entries.translation:
那男人接受了他們的同伴身分。
@0跟這個看起來粗獷的傢伙隨口閒聊，@1在一旁看著，留意著別讓這位法師一時興奮就洩漏了他們此行的真正目的。
「那，你們要去哪？」男人問道，用酒杯比劃了個大圈。「有什麼有趣的地方嗎？」
「其實我們沒有ñ特定的方向，」@1插話道。「我們就是四處走走。找個雇主。看守寶物、護送商隊之類的……」
男人竊笑了一聲。「還是打劫商隊？那是自由兵囉。這年頭王國其實沒什麼油水，尤其在西邊。親王把路修得太平安，屬下也養得太安逸了。像我們這種人，日子都被他弄得沒滋沒味了。」
@4點了點頭。「說這話的可不只你一個。」�

entries.source:
@4 slapped the man on the back.
Immediately he regretted doing so as the mercenary gasped, his face contorting into a mask of pain.
"I'm sorry. I didn't realize...Is your shoulder broken?" @4 asked.
"Don't worry yourself about it," the man spat between gritted teeth. "I haven't exactly made the fact known." A faint popping sound issued from the man's back as he moved his shoulder, tears forming in the corners of his eyes. "I was a courier for the dwarves. I reasoned there would be less chance a brigand would try to intercept me if he wasn't aware I was injured."
@4 nodded sympathetically. "Did you break it in a fight?"
"No, a fall," the man said. "Stupid man I am, I was in the dwarven caves and I came to this pit---part of the caves had collapsed so there were all kinds of sinkholes everywhere. Since there wasn't a plank I could walk over and I didn't have any kind of rope...I jumped. I think if I had the chance to make the decision again, I'd have waited until I got my hands on a coil of hemp."�

entries.translation:
@4拍了拍男人的背。
他立刻後悔了，只見那傭兵倒抽一口氣，臉部因劇痛而扭曲。
「抱歉，我沒注意到……你的肩膀是不是斷了？」@4問道。
「別擔心，」男人咬牙切齒地啐了一句。「我還沒讓大家知道這件事。」他活動肩膀時，背後傳來一聲輕微的骨頭錯位聲，眼角泛起淚光。「我以前替矮人送信。我想著，要是沒人知道我受了傷，強盜想半路攔截我的機會也會小一點。」
@4同情地點了點頭。「是打鬥時弄傷的嗎？」
「不，是摔的，」男人說。「我真是個笨蛋，我當時在矮人的坑道裡，走到一處坑洞——那邊有段坑道塌了，到處都是坑坑洞洞的陷坑。因為沒有木板可以走過去，我身上也沒帶繩子……我就這麼跳了下去。要是能重新選一次，我大概會等到找到一捆麻繩再說。」�

entries.source:
The man waved them over.
@4 made no hurry of approaching the man, taking time to make note of several things, not the least of which was that three different knife hilts protruded from under the man's leather belt. The man was a bounty hunter.
"We appear to be of mutual interest," @4 said.
"You seem a little out of place," the man said, narrowing his gaze. "You'll not be traders because you didn't offer me a drink. It also seems unlikely you are mercenaries because you don't have their smell on you. So what is it then? Vagabonds, beggars...traitors?"
@4 smiled dangerously. "If you imagine a jingle in your pouch for claiming our heads, let me reassure you, you'll have only skulls for your efforts. There are no blood prices upon us, hunter. Of course, I wouldn't expect you to take us at our word."
"Of course not," the man replied, returning the smile. "You won't mind that I ask a few of the other patrons here if they recognize your faces?"
@4 motioned to the bar. "Please, be our ñguestð."�

entries.translation:
那男人朝他們揮了揮手。
@4不慌不忙地走近那男人，趁機留意了幾件事，其中最顯眼的是，他皮帶下露出三把不同刀柄。這男人是個賞金獵人。
「看來我們彼此有共同的興趣，」@4說道。
「你看起來不太對勁，」男人瞇起眼說道。「你們不像商人，因為沒請我喝酒。也不太像傭兵，因為你們身上沒那股味道。那到底是什麼？流浪漢、乞丐……還是叛徒？」
@4露出危險的笑容。「如果你以為砍下我們的頭能賺到什麼叮噹作響的賞金，我可以老實告訴你，你頂多只會落得一堆空歡喜。我們身上可沒有懸賞，獵人先生。當然，我也不指望你會就這樣相信我們的話。」
「那是自然，」男人回以笑容說道。「你們不介意我去問問這裡其他幾位客人，看他們認不認得你們的臉吧？」
@4朝吧台示意。「請便，就當ñ自己家ð。」�
